ly learn how this industry  is working if you're not working at the  studio system  what would you say is the sweet spot  that an independent filmmaker should  spend on their movie i think a sweet  spot for an independent filmmaker is  it's different for everybody because  content different content drives more  dollars internationally you know comedy  if it's circumstantial comedy that's one  thing but if it's it's written comedy it  doesn't always translate foreign so  you're limiting your foreign  certain films don't do well overseas so  i don't think there's a sweet spot for  everybody i think there are sweet spots  that people can do  and if you're going to spend more money  just put it in the cast it really is  it's if there's content there's content  that fits a niche or a genre but then  there's also star power and if you're  trying to get a-list actors they're  always going to cost you a lot of money  so you know some independent filmmakers  do very well they'll make three or four  million dollar films they'll put two  million dollars into two actors and then  everything else is you know the rest of  the film there's nothing wrong with that  um  if you're doing you know the walk and  talk dramas i you know unless you're  you're knocking it out of the park with  star power why do these films need to be  made for more than three hundred  thousand dollars i just i don't know why  they would need to be if you're not if  you are not justifying it with the star  power  again  spend 10 million if you're getting  george clooney and meg ryan or whoever's  hot today you know it changes every  other day  that's justifiable globally that's going  to do a lot for your revenue but if  you're working with  actors that are really good at their  craft that that are blue collar actors  that are going to get the job done but  they're not marquee  you know you really got to think about  how you can keep the costs down because  again the less you spend the less you're  going to 